# .gitignore - files git must never track (they never get committed).
#
# - .env holds your real API keys: committing it would leak them (.env.example is the template).
# - __pycache__/, *.pyc: compiled Python files, recreated automatically.
# - .venv/, .pytest_cache/, .langgraph_api/: local tool folders (virtualenv, pytest, LangGraph Studio).
# - evals/audio/: your recorded answers (SAVE_AUDIO=true), large and personal.
# - brief_edit.json: temporary file the CLI writes when you edit a brief by hand.
# - my_docs/: your real CV, job posts and recruiter emails (personal data). Keep them here,
#   not in samples/, which is committed and holds fictional examples only.
# - evals/private/: eval cases built from your real answers; evals/*/runs/: local eval summaries.
# - Terraform (infra/): .terraform/ (downloaded providers), *.tfstate (the bootstrap's local
#   state), terraform.tfvars (your email) and backend.hcl (the state bucket's name, with your
#   AWS account id), *.tfplan (saved plans), *.auto.tfvars (server.ps1's on/off switch). .terraform.lock.hcl IS committed: it pins the provider versions.

.env
my_docs/
evals/private/
evals/*/runs/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
.pytest_cache/
.langgraph_api/
evals/audio/
brief_edit.json
.terraform/
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
terraform.tfvars
infra/backend.hcl
*.tfplan
*.auto.tfvars
